.SH "BUGS"
The library uses \fBeval\fR to execute wrapped applications, which may cause unexpected word splitting if arguments contain unusual characters\.
.P
Version comparison in \fBrecord_require_minimum\fR is only performed when both the required and actual values match the dotted\-numeric or magnitude\-suffix patterns; non\-matching strings cause the function to return non\-zero via the regex fall\-through path\.
.P
The \fBRECORD_PIPELINE\fR file is written to \fB/tmp\fR using a name derived from \fB$USER\fR, \fB$$\fR, and \fB$(basename $0)\fR, which may cause collisions in unusual execution environments\.
